> Indonesia - Eko Nugroho and "Wayang Boc[or]"
Eko Nurgoho is one[ of] Indonesia's most provocative young artists whose style is a[ unique] mix[ of] Indonesia's rich traditions and popular culture t[inged] with dark humor. Using a distinctive blend of high[ and] low art, Nugroho' "Wayang B[oc]or" is a contemporary form of theater in[ which] puppets and actors weave[ together][ traditional] elements of Indonesian 'wayag' (shadow[ pupp]ets) with live theater and scripts that cast a satiric view of[ contemporary] subjects. The show "God Bliss" tells the story of[ how] Islam came to[ Java], and became[ absorbed][ as] part of Javanese culture that includes elements of[ Hindu]ism, Buddhism, and[ anim][ism]. Simultaneously playful and penetrating.

